In order to demonstrate the computational efficiency of the algorithm, we have compared the CPU time used by the OCS2 algorithm with the baseline method introduced by Xu and Antsaklis (2004). We observe that as the dimensions of state and input spaces increase, the difference in computational time between the algorithms becomes significant to the point that for the quadruped CoM control task, the run-time of the baseline algorithm becomes prohibitively long.
